# Files that must never reach GitHub.
#
# WARNING - an ignore rule has NO effect on a file git ALREADY TRACKS.
# .claude/CLAUDE.md proves it: it is matched by a rule below and is public anyway, because it
# was committed before the rule existed. For an already-tracked file the only fix is
# "git rm --cached <file>", which Gabriel runs in GitHub Desktop. Claude never writes git history here.
#
# WARNING - a comment must sit on its own line. Git has no end-of-line comments: it reads
# "pattern   # note" as one pattern, note included, and that pattern matches no file.
#
# The decision about which SKILLS are published lives in one file:
#   C:\Users\trei\.claude\skills\publish-list.md
# The generated block at the bottom of this file is only a second net. Regenerate both together.

# ---------- single files ----------
# The root CLAUDE.md holds internal notes. Every OTHER CLAUDE.md in this repo IS published.
/CLAUDE.md
PUBLISH-PROTOCOL.md
publish-list.md
.claude/skills/HowWeShareTheseSkills.md

# ---------- internal by nature, at any depth ----------
# descript.ion - Total Commander folder comments. Local file-manager artefact.
descript.ion
# HandOver.md - cross-session memory: what is unfinished, blocked, broken.
HandOver.md
# todo.md - the backlog, including everything broken and not fixed yet.
todo.md
# session-*.md - throwaway notes for one task.
session-*.md
# evals/ - test cases built out of our own past mistakes, and they quote them.
evals/
# history/ - kept precisely because it records what went wrong.
history/

# A skill’s own CLAUDE.md is its private notes on how it was wrong. One level only, so this does
# NOT match .claude/skills/CLAUDE.md, which is a separately written public file and IS published.
.claude/skills/*/CLAUDE.md

